This file is a placeholder. It is not committed on purpose.

The real document served from this path is Konami's actual MGO Online
User Agreement text -- the console fetches it verbatim from here (see
dev/docs/OBSERVED.md), and we have a real extracted copy, but it is not
ours to redistribute, so it is gitignored rather than checked in.

Unlike the game's own help/tips documents, this file has no <title> or
<page-break> markup -- the real policy.txt is plain text, read by a
different part of the client than the TIPS panel.

Without a real copy in its place, a client fetching this path gets the
dev harness's generic "document not found" fallback instead, which on
real hardware shows up as being stuck on the terms/network screen (see
dev/docs/SETUP.md, "Verifying the pieces").

To fix it: copy your own extracted copy of policy.txt into this same
directory, named policy.txt (not .txt.example). Nothing else needs to
change; the path is already wired up and gitignored.
